# 3. Device Drivers

A device driver is software that allows the operating system to communicate with and control a hardware device.

Example:

```text
Windows
   ↓
Network Driver
   ↓
Network Adapter
   ↓
Network
```

Without an appropriate driver, Windows may not be able to properly communicate with the hardware.

