# 7. Group Policy

Group Policy allows administrators to centrally apply configuration and security settings to users and computers in a Windows domain environment.

### Examples

* Security settings
* Password policies
* Desktop restrictions
* Windows configuration
* User settings
* Computer settings

### Basic Structure

```text
Active Directory
       ↓
Group Policy
       ↓
Users / Computers
       ↓
Configuration Applied
```

Group Policy can be applied to users or computers based on their location and membership within an Active Directory environment.

