# 8. `gpupdate`

`gpupdate` is used to refresh Group Policy settings.

### Command

```cmd
gpupdate /force
```

The `/force` option causes policy settings to be reapplied, including settings that have not changed.

### Basic Concept

```text
gpupdate
↓
Refresh / reapply Group Policy
```

---

# 9. `gpresult`

`gpresult` displays Resultant Set of Policy (RSoP) information showing Group Policy settings that are applied to a user or computer.

### Command

```cmd
gpresult /r
```

### Concept

```text
gpupdate
↓
Refresh policy

gpresult
↓
Check resulting/applied policy
```

Microsoft documents `gpresult` as a tool for displaying the resulting Group Policy settings enforced for a user and computer.

