# 10. GPO Troubleshooting

### Scenario

> User reports that a new company policy is not being applied.

### Troubleshooting Process

```text
Gather Information
↓
Determine whether one or multiple users are affected
↓
Check whether computer is domain-connected
↓
Check User / Computer OU
↓
Check GPO link
↓
Check security filtering
↓
Run gpupdate /force
↓
Run gpresult /r
↓
Review Event Viewer if necessary
↓
Verify with user
↓
Document
↓
Escalate if required
```

Microsoft's Group Policy troubleshooting guidance recommends reviewing Group Policy event logs, refreshing policy with `GPUPDATE`, and using `GPRESULT` to examine the resulting policy.

