# 11. Linux Package Management

Linux systems such as Ubuntu use package managers to manage software.

### `apt update`

```bash
sudo apt update
```

This updates the local package information from configured repositories.

It does **not** upgrade installed packages.

### `apt upgrade`

```bash
sudo apt upgrade
```

This installs available newer versions of installed packages.

### Installing a Package

```bash
sudo apt install <package-name>
```

Example:

```bash
sudo apt install tree
```

### Remember

```text
apt update
↓
Update package information

apt upgrade
↓
Upgrade installed packages

apt install
↓
Install a package
```

