# 12. Linux Logs

Many Linux logs are stored under:

```text
/var/log
```

### Important Correction

The correct common log directory is:

```text
/var/log
```

Not:

```text
/etc/var
```

### Explore Logs

```bash
ls /var/log
```

Logs can contain information about:

* Authentication
* System activity
* Services
* Applications
* Errors

Logs are important because they provide evidence about what happened on the system.

