# 13. `grep`

`grep` is used to search text for matching patterns.

Example:

```bash
grep "error" logfile
```

Another example:

```bash
grep -i "failed" /var/log/auth.log
```

The `-i` option performs a case-insensitive search.

### Concept

```text
grep
↓
Search / filter text
```

The Linux `grep` utility searches files for lines matching a specified pattern.

