# 16. DHCP Troubleshooting

DHCP automatically provides network configuration information to clients.

Common information includes:

* IP address
* Subnet mask
* Default gateway
* DNS server

### Windows Command

```cmd
ipconfig /all
```

Look for:

```text
DHCP Enabled
IPv4 Address
Subnet Mask
Default Gateway
DNS Servers
```

### Renew DHCP Configuration

```cmd
ipconfig /release
```

Then:

```cmd
ipconfig /renew
```

Use these commands appropriately and understand that releasing the lease temporarily removes the current DHCP configuration.

