# 17. Default Gateway

A default gateway is normally a router or Layer 3 interface that forwards traffic from a host's local network toward other networks when there is no more specific route.

Example:

```text
Computer
   ↓
Default Gateway
   ↓
Router
   ↓
Other Network
   ↓
Internet
```

### Check in Windows

```cmd
ipconfig
```

### Test Gateway

```cmd
ping <default-gateway>
```

