# 24. Key Technical Corrections From Day 46

### Event Viewer

> Windows utility for viewing and analyzing event logs.

### Device Manager

> Windows utility for managing hardware devices and drivers.

### Driver

> Software that allows Windows to communicate with hardware.

### BSOD

> A critical Windows system error; BSOD itself is a symptom, not the root cause.

### System Restore

> Returns certain system configuration/system-state components to an earlier restore point; it is not a personal-file backup.

### Group Policy

> Centrally applies configuration and security settings to users and computers.

### `gpupdate`

> Refreshes/reapplies Group Policy.

### `gpresult`

> Displays the resulting/applied Group Policy information.

### Linux logs

```text
/var/log
```

### `grep`

> Searches text for matching patterns.

### Default Gateway

> Forwards traffic toward other networks when no more specific route exists.

### ARP

> Resolves/maps IPv4 addresses to MAC addresses on the local network.

### `nslookup`

> Queries DNS.

### `tracert`

> Shows network hops toward a destination.

